package Libraries.Game.Graphics.Trees

use Libraries.Game.BoundingBox
use Libraries.Interface.Item3D
use Libraries.Compute.Math
use Libraries.Compute.Matrix4
use Libraries.Compute.Vector3

/*
RenderTreeNode3D is the record a render tree keeps for each item: the item,
its bounds, and which half of the tree it is in. It is called a leaf.

In a RenderBoundingVolumeTree3D, nodes are also the tree itself. A node is
either a leaf, which holds one drawable item and the box around it, or a
branch, which holds two children and the box around both. The parent, left,
right and height fields are used only there.

In a RenderCellTree3D, used by QuadTree3D and Octree3D, a leaf instead records
the cell it is in and its place in that cell's list, so it can be removed
without searching.

Only the tree classes in this package should change a node. The node also
does the box calculations the trees need, such as finding its item's bounds
in the world, so each tree asks the node rather than sharing private
helpers.

A node's box can be read two ways. GetBounds returns the node's own box,
not a copy, so changing it changes the node. The tree uses it to update
boxes in place without making new objects. GetBoundsCopy returns a new box
with the same corners, which can be changed freely, but makes a new object
on every call.

Attribute: Example

use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Trees.DynamicVolumeRenderTree3D
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Trees.RenderTreeNode3D
use Libraries.Interface.Item3D

DynamicVolumeRenderTree3D tree
Item3D box
box:SetDimensions(1, 1, 1)
tree:Add(box)

// Keep the leaf, so moves need no lookup.
RenderTreeNode3D leaf = tree:GetLeaf(box)
box:SetPosition(2, 0, 0)
tree:Moved(leaf)
output leaf:GetBounds():GetCenterX()
*/
class RenderTreeNode3D
    // The box this node covers. For a leaf in the dynamic half of the tree it
    // is a little bigger than the item, so small moves do not change the tree.
    BoundingBox bounds

    RenderTreeNode3D parentNode = undefined
    RenderTreeNode3D left = undefined
    RenderTreeNode3D right = undefined

    // How many levels are below this node. A leaf is 0.
    integer height = 0

    // The item a leaf holds. Branches hold no item.
    Item3D item = undefined

    // Whether the leaf is in the static half of the tree.
    boolean isStatic = false

    // The frame the leaf last moved on, used to move still items back to
    // the static half.
    integer lastMovedFrame = 0

    // The last frame the owner handed this leaf's item to be drawn, kept by
    // the owner, such as Layer3D, so an item found by more than one search
    // in a frame is only drawn once.
    integer lastDrawnFrame = -1

    // The cell of a RenderCellTree3D the leaf is in, and its place in the
    // cell's list of leaves. A leaf in the cell tree's list of leaves outside
    // its region has no cell, but still has a place in that list.
    RenderTreeCell3D cell = undefined
    integer cellIndex = -1

    // The item's bounds in its own coordinates, as a center and half sizes.
    // They are turned into world bounds each time the item moves.
    number localCenterX = 0
    number localCenterY = 0
    number localCenterZ = 0
    number localHalfX = 0
    number localHalfY = 0
    number localHalfZ = 0

    Math math

    /*
    This action returns the box this node covers. The box itself is
    returned, not a copy, so changing it changes the node. The tree uses
    this to update boxes in place without making new objects. To look at
    the box without any risk of changing the node, use GetBoundsCopy.

    Attribute: Returns The node's own box, not a copy.
    */
    action GetBounds returns BoundingBox
        return bounds
    end

    /*
    This action returns a new box with the same corners as the box this
    node covers. Changing the copy does not change the node. Each call makes
    a new object, so code that runs every frame should use GetBounds
    instead, and only read from it.

    Attribute: Returns A copy of the node's box.
    */
    action GetBoundsCopy returns BoundingBox
        return bounds:Copy()
    end

    /*
    This action returns the branch above this node, or undefined if this node
    is the root or is in a RenderCellTree3D.

    Attribute: Returns The branch above this node, or undefined.
    */
    action GetParentNode returns RenderTreeNode3D
        return parentNode
    end

    /*
    This action sets the branch above this node.

    Attribute: Parameter node The branch above this node, or undefined for the
    root.
    */
    action SetParentNode(RenderTreeNode3D node)
        parentNode = node
    end

    /*
    This action returns the first child of a branch, or undefined for a leaf.

    Attribute: Returns The first child, or undefined.
    */
    action GetLeft returns RenderTreeNode3D
        return left
    end

    /*
    This action sets the first child of a branch.

    Attribute: Parameter node The first child, or undefined to make this node a
    leaf.
    */
    action SetLeft(RenderTreeNode3D node)
        left = node
    end

    /*
    This action returns the second child of a branch, or undefined for a leaf.

    Attribute: Returns The second child, or undefined.
    */
    action GetRight returns RenderTreeNode3D
        return right
    end

    /*
    This action sets the second child of a branch.

    Attribute: Parameter node The second child, or undefined for a leaf.
    */
    action SetRight(RenderTreeNode3D node)
        right = node
    end

    /*
    This action returns how many levels are below this node. A leaf is 0.

    Attribute: Returns The number of levels below this node.
    */
    action GetHeight returns integer
        return height
    end

    /*
    This action sets how many levels are below this node.

    Attribute: Parameter value The number of levels below this node.
    */
    action SetHeight(integer value)
        height = value
    end

    /*
    This action returns the item a leaf holds, or undefined for a branch or
    for a leaf whose item has been removed.

    Attribute: Returns The item, or undefined.
    */
    action GetItem returns Item3D
        return item
    end

    /*
    This action sets the item a leaf holds.

    Attribute: Parameter value The item.
    */
    action SetItem(Item3D value)
        item = value
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the leaf is in the static half of the tree.

    Attribute: Returns True if the leaf is static.
    */
    action IsStatic returns boolean
        return isStatic
    end

    /*
    This action sets whether the leaf is in the static half of the tree.

    Attribute: Parameter value True if the leaf is static.
    */
    action SetStatic(boolean value)
        isStatic = value
    end

    /*
    This action returns the frame the leaf last moved on. The tree uses it to
    move still items back to the static half.

    Attribute: Returns The frame number.
    */
    action GetLastMovedFrame returns integer
        return lastMovedFrame
    end

    /*
    This action sets the frame the leaf last moved on.

    Attribute: Parameter frame The frame number.
    */
    action SetLastMovedFrame(integer frame)
        lastMovedFrame = frame
    end

    /*
    This action returns the last frame the leaf's item was handed to be
    drawn, or -1 if it never has been. The tree does not use this. It is
    kept for the tree's owner, such as Layer3D, so an item found by more than
    one search in a frame is only drawn once.

    Attribute: Returns The frame number, or -1.
    */
    action GetLastDrawnFrame returns integer
        return lastDrawnFrame
    end

    /*
    This action sets the last frame the leaf's item was handed to be drawn.

    Attribute: Parameter frame The frame number.
    */
    action SetLastDrawnFrame(integer frame)
        lastDrawnFrame = frame
    end

    /*
    This action returns the RenderCellTree3D cell the leaf is in, or
    undefined if it is in none.

    Attribute: Returns The cell, or undefined.
    */
    action GetCell returns RenderTreeCell3D
        return cell
    end

    /*
    This action sets the RenderCellTree3D cell the leaf is in.

    Attribute: Parameter value The cell, or undefined if the leaf is in none.
    */
    action SetCell(RenderTreeCell3D value)
        cell = value
    end

    /*
    This action returns the leaf's place in its cell's list of leaves, or in
    the cell tree's list of leaves outside its region, or -1 if it is in
    neither.

    Attribute: Returns The leaf's place, or -1.
    */
    action GetCellIndex returns integer
        return cellIndex
    end

    /*
    This action sets the leaf's place in its cell's list of leaves, or in the
    cell tree's list of leaves outside its region.

    Attribute: Parameter index The leaf's place, or -1 if it is in neither.
    */
    action SetCellIndex(integer index)
        cellIndex = index
    end

    /*
    This action returns the x coordinate of the center of the item's bounds,
    in the item's own coordinates. It is set with SetLocalBounds.

    Attribute: Returns The x coordinate of the center.
    */
    action GetLocalCenterX returns number
        return localCenterX
    end

    /*
    This action returns the y coordinate of the center of the item's bounds,
    in the item's own coordinates. It is set with SetLocalBounds.

    Attribute: Returns The y coordinate of the center.
    */
    action GetLocalCenterY returns number
        return localCenterY
    end

    /*
    This action returns the z coordinate of the center of the item's bounds,
    in the item's own coordinates. It is set with SetLocalBounds.

    Attribute: Returns The z coordinate of the center.
    */
    action GetLocalCenterZ returns number
        return localCenterZ
    end

    /*
    This action returns half the size of the item's bounds along x, in the
    item's own coordinates. It is set with SetLocalBounds.

    Attribute: Returns Half the size along x.
    */
    action GetLocalHalfX returns number
        return localHalfX
    end

    /*
    This action returns half the size of the item's bounds along y, in the
    item's own coordinates. It is set with SetLocalBounds.

    Attribute: Returns Half the size along y.
    */
    action GetLocalHalfY returns number
        return localHalfY
    end

    /*
    This action returns half the size of the item's bounds along z, in the
    item's own coordinates. It is set with SetLocalBounds.

    Attribute: Returns Half the size along z.
    */
    action GetLocalHalfZ returns number
        return localHalfZ
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if this node is a leaf, which holds an item,
    and false if it is a branch.

    Attribute: Returns True if this node is a leaf.
    */
    action IsLeaf returns boolean
        return left = undefined
    end

    /*
    This action clears the node so it can be reused for another item or
    branch.
    */
    action Reset
        parentNode = undefined
        left = undefined
        right = undefined
        height = 0
        item = undefined
        isStatic = false
        lastMovedFrame = 0
        lastDrawnFrame = -1
        cell = undefined
        cellIndex = -1
        bounds:Invalidate()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the item's bounds in its own coordinates. They are kept
    as a center and half sizes, and turned into world bounds each time the
    item moves.

    Attribute: Parameter local The item's bounds in its own coordinates.
    */
    action SetLocalBounds(BoundingBox local)
        localCenterX = local:GetCenterX()
        localCenterY = local:GetCenterY()
        localCenterZ = local:GetCenterZ()
        localHalfX = local:GetWidth() / 2
        localHalfY = local:GetHeight() / 2
        localHalfZ = local:GetDepth() / 2
    end

    /*
    This action sets the node's box to the item's bounds, made bigger by
    the margin on every side.

    Attribute: Parameter itemBounds The item's bounds in the world.
    Attribute: Parameter margin How much bigger to make the box on every side.
    */
    action SetBounds(BoundingBox itemBounds, number margin)
        Vector3 itemMinimum = itemBounds:GetMinimum()
        Vector3 itemMaximum = itemBounds:GetMaximum()
        bounds:GetMinimum():Set(itemMinimum:GetX() - margin, itemMinimum:GetY() - margin, itemMinimum:GetZ() - margin)
        bounds:GetMaximum():Set(itemMaximum:GetX() + margin, itemMaximum:GetY() + margin, itemMaximum:GetZ() + margin)
        bounds:CalculateDimensions()
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the node's box holds all of the given box.
    Equal edges count as inside, so a flat item, such as a plane, fits a
    box of the same size.

    Attribute: Parameter box The box to test.
    Attribute: Returns True if the node's box holds all of it.
    */
    action Contains(BoundingBox box) returns boolean
        Vector3 outerMinimum = bounds:GetMinimum()
        Vector3 outerMaximum = bounds:GetMaximum()
        Vector3 innerMinimum = box:GetMinimum()
        Vector3 innerMaximum = box:GetMaximum()
        return outerMinimum:GetX() <= innerMinimum:GetX() and
            outerMinimum:GetY() <= innerMinimum:GetY() and
            outerMinimum:GetZ() <= innerMinimum:GetZ() and
            innerMaximum:GetX() <= outerMaximum:GetX() and
            innerMaximum:GetY() <= outerMaximum:GetY() and
            innerMaximum:GetZ() <= outerMaximum:GetZ()
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the node's box has the same corners as the
    given box.

    Attribute: Parameter box The box to compare with.
    Attribute: Returns True if the corners are the same.
    */
    action HasBounds(BoundingBox box) returns boolean
        return bounds:GetMinimum():GetX() = box:GetMinimum():GetX() and
            bounds:GetMinimum():GetY() = box:GetMinimum():GetY() and
            bounds:GetMinimum():GetZ() = box:GetMinimum():GetZ() and
            bounds:GetMaximum():GetX() = box:GetMaximum():GetX() and
            bounds:GetMaximum():GetY() = box:GetMaximum():GetY() and
            bounds:GetMaximum():GetZ() = box:GetMaximum():GetZ()
    end

    /*
    This action returns the squared distance from a point to the nearest
    point of the node's box, which is 0 when the point is inside it.

    Attribute: Parameter x The point's x coordinate.
    Attribute: Parameter y The point's y coordinate.
    Attribute: Parameter z The point's z coordinate.
    Attribute: Returns The squared distance.
    */
    action DistanceSquared(number x, number y, number z) returns number
        Vector3 boxMinimum = bounds:GetMinimum()
        Vector3 boxMaximum = bounds:GetMaximum()
        number dx = 0
        number dy = 0
        number dz = 0
        if x < boxMinimum:GetX()
            dx = boxMinimum:GetX() - x
        elseif x > boxMaximum:GetX()
            dx = x - boxMaximum:GetX()
        end
        if y < boxMinimum:GetY()
            dy = boxMinimum:GetY() - y
        elseif y > boxMaximum:GetY()
            dy = y - boxMaximum:GetY()
        end
        if z < boxMinimum:GetZ()
            dz = boxMinimum:GetZ() - z
        elseif z > boxMaximum:GetZ()
            dz = z - boxMaximum:GetZ()
        end
        return dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz
    end

    /*
    This action puts the leaf's item's bounds in world coordinates into the
    given box.

    The item's bounds in its own coordinates are a center and half sizes.
    The world center is the item's transform applied to the center. The
    world half size on each axis is the sum of the absolute values of the
    transform's entries in that row, each times the matching half size. This
    is the smallest axis-aligned box around the turned box, and needs no
    corners. The transform includes the item's scale and its parent's offset.

    Attribute: Parameter out The box to put the world bounds in.
    */
    action CalculateWorldBounds(BoundingBox out)
        Matrix4 transform = item:GetTransform()

        number worldX = transform:row0column0 * localCenterX + transform:row0column1 * localCenterY +
            transform:row0column2 * localCenterZ + transform:row0column3
        number worldY = transform:row1column0 * localCenterX + transform:row1column1 * localCenterY +
            transform:row1column2 * localCenterZ + transform:row1column3
        number worldZ = transform:row2column0 * localCenterX + transform:row2column1 * localCenterY +
            transform:row2column2 * localCenterZ + transform:row2column3

        number halfX = math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row0column0) * localHalfX + math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row0column1) * localHalfY +
            math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row0column2) * localHalfZ
        number halfY = math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row1column0) * localHalfX + math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row1column1) * localHalfY +
            math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row1column2) * localHalfZ
        number halfZ = math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row2column0) * localHalfX + math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row2column1) * localHalfY +
            math:AbsoluteValue(transform:row2column2) * localHalfZ

        out:GetMinimum():Set(worldX - halfX, worldY - halfY, worldZ - halfZ)
        out:GetMaximum():Set(worldX + halfX, worldY + halfY, worldZ + halfZ)
        out:CalculateDimensions()
    end
end
